        "original_id": "9e91e4d8-505f-5ce8-9c97-85d8f7a69513",
        "text": "This chunk explains the term “Cadillac insurance plan” and its connection to U.S. health policy debates.\n\nThis chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Cadillac insurance plan\n- Events: Debate over the Clinton health care plan\n- Projects: Clinton health care plan, 1993 healthcare reform package\n- People: Bill Clinton\n- Places: United States\n- Topics: Medical-cost control measures, health insurance\n\nFacts:\n- A Cadillac insurance plan is an unusually expensive health insurance plan.\n- The term Cadillac insurance plan usually arises in discussions of medical-cost control measures in the United States.\n- In the early 1990s, the term Cadillac insurance plan gained popularity during the debate over the Clinton health care plan.\n- In 1993, the Clinton health care plan was a healthcare reform package proposed by the administration of U.S. President Bill Clinton.\n- The Clinton health care plan was closely associated with the chair of the task force that devised the plan.",
